{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And the angels of Elohim met him.</b> This is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Genesis 32:2): Angels of the land of Israel came forth to meet him. \"Mahanaim\" — two camps: the camp from outside the land that had come with him thus far, and the camp of the land of Israel that came forth to meet him. But I am astonished by this, for Jacob had not yet reached the land and was far from there, and he sent messengers to Esau from afar, and there (Genesis 32:23) it says, \"And he crossed the ford of Jabbok,\" which is \"the Jabbok river, the border of the children of Ammon\" (Deuteronomy 3:16), which is southeast of the land of Israel, and he still had to pass through the territory of the children of Ammon and Moab, and after that the land of Edom, and the beginning of his entry into the land was at Shechem, as it says (Genesis 33:18), \"And Jacob came safely to the city of Shechem, which is in the land of Canaan.\" Rather, this vision appeared to Jacob when he came into the territory of his enemies, to inform him that those who were with him were more numerous than those with them. And the place was named Mahanaim because such is the way with names, or \"Mahanaim\" — his camp and the camp of the supernal beings, to say that his camp on earth was like the camp of the angels, all of them camps of Elohim, blessing him and proclaiming the unity of His name, may His name be blessed forever." "Thus concludes the pericah of Vayetze."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:38:12.050874261Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}